<Docs title="Typography" active="typography" description="Fluid reading sizes, stable self-hosted families and explicit readability floors."><section class="docs-card"><h2>Reading scale</h2><p>Body: 16–18px fluid Inter, 1.65 line height and up to 68ch. UI metadata: 14px minimum. Reserve 12px for limited legal/caption uses, not navigation or forms.</p><p>Display: 40–72px fluid Barlow Condensed. Component titles stay at least 20px. Spacing endpoints use a 4px grid; intermediate type sizes and letter spacing do not need to be divisible by four.</p><p>Caveat is an occasional annotation, not body text. On light surfaces use a contrast-verified dark foreground rather than Amber. JetBrains Mono supports code and metadata.</p><h3>Fonts</h3><p>Existing static Barlow Condensed files remain self-hosted with font-display: swap. A variable Barlow Condensed file has not been verified; do not invent its availability or claim a fixed font-payload budget without measurement.</p><pre><code>{`font-size: clamp(1rem, .95rem + .25vw, 1.125rem);
line-height: 1.65;
max-inline-size: 68ch;`}</code></pre><button data-copy="font-size: clamp(1rem, .95rem + .25vw, 1.125rem); line-height: 1.65; max-inline-size: 68ch;">Copy reading CSS</button><p class="copy-status" role="status"></p></section><details class="docs-card"><summary>Existing type specimens and migration reference</summary><p>Historical specimen tables illustrate existing tokens; migrate smaller legacy labels to the reading floors above. They do not override the current accessible component specification.</p><div class="legacy-example"><TypographySystem client:visible/></div></details></Docs>
